    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Normalize incoming Vapi payload into flat fields\nconst body = $input.first().json.body || $input.first().json;\nconst args = body.message?.toolCalls?.[0]?.function?.arguments\n  || body.message?.functionCall?.parameters\n  || body.functionCall?.parameters\n  || body;\n\nfunction parseBudget(raw) {\n  if (typeof raw === 'number') return raw;\n  if (!raw) return 0;\n\n  const str = String(raw).toLowerCase().trim();\n\n  // Remove thousands-separator commas between digits (e.g. \"600,000\" -> \"600000\")\n  const noCommas = str.replace(/(\\d),(?=\\d)/g, '$1');\n\n  // Extract the FIRST number only (handles ranges like \"2 to 3 lakhs\" -> takes 2)\n  const match = noCommas.match(/[0-9]+(\\.[0-9]+)?/);\n  if (!match) return 0;\n  let num = parseFloat(match[0]);\n\n  if (noCommas.includes('crore')) return num * 10000000;\n  if (noCommas.includes('lakh') || noCommas.includes('lac')) return num * 100000;\n  if (/\\bk\\b|[0-9]k\\b/.test(noCommas)) return num * 1000;\n\n  return num;\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    client_name: args.client_name || args.name || '',\n    company: args.company_name || args.company || '',\n    email: args.email || '',\n    service: args.service_required || args.service || '',\n    description: args.project_description || args.description || '',\n    budget: parseBudget(args.budget)\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "id": "d7ad30af-2ae0-4f55-be92-e6fc84c86571",
      "name": "Normalize Client Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -368,
        192
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Classify this client intake request.\n\nClient Name: {{ $json.client_name }}\nCompany: {{ $json.company }}\nService Requested: {{ $json.service }}\nProject Description: {{ $json.description }}\nBudget (PKR): {{ $json.budget }}\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object (no markdown, no code fences, no explanation) with exactly these 4 fields:\n- service_category: a short category name for the requested service\n- priority: HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW, following this exact logic — Budget >= 500000 -> HIGH, Budget 200000 to 499999 -> MEDIUM, Budget < 200000 -> LOW\n- summary: one short sentence summarizing what the client needs\n- next_action: a short recommended next step for the team\n\nExample output:\n{\"service_category\": \"Web & Mobile Development\", \"priority\": \"HIGH\", \"summary\": \"Restaurant requires website and mobile ordering application.\", \"next_action\": \"Schedule technical consultation\"}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a strict lead classification assistant for a business onboarding pipeline. You always respond with ONLY raw JSON — never markdown, never code fences, never extra commentary. Apply the priority logic exactly as instructed; do not deviate from the budget thresholds given."
        }
      },
      "id": "c40bf342-be27-4204-bf34-0d92e516a4b8",
      "name": "AI Agent - Classify Lead",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
